22 0 obj
<<
/A 169 0 R
/Alt (Flowchart illustrating a study design. Out of 137 healthy subjects assessed, 81 were excluded due to various reasons like abnormal lab values and voluntary withdrawal. The remaining 56 were enrolled and randomly assigned to fasting \(28\) or fed \(28\) groups. Both groups were further split into T and R groups, each with 14 subjects for each period. In the second period, one from the Fed R group shows poor adherence.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 16 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
23 0 obj
<<
/A 169 0 R
/Alt (Two chromatograms display intensity versus time, each with a sharp blue peak around 2.5 minutes. The left chromatogram peaks at 2.537, the right at 2.534. Details like sample type and times are visible above each graph.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 17 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
24 0 obj
<<
/A 169 0 R
/Alt (Two line graphs compare Everolimus tablet concentrations in fasting \(A\) and fed \(B\) states over time. Graph A \(fasting state\) shows a peak concentration near 35 ng/mL, whereas Graph B \(fed state\) shows a lower peak near 15 ng/mL, Both graphs demonstrate a decline in drug concentration, exhibiting near-complete elimination \(approximately 95% clearance\) within 100 hours. Legends indicate different test conditions with solid and dashed lines representing two treatment lines labeled T and R.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 18 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
